Water safety plan manual — WHO and IWA, second edition (@wu-wsp: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_3JMZKS3FG80FKX9YRQPEJMA4VD
World Health Organization and International Water Association. Water safety plan manual: step-by-step risk management for drinking-water suppliers, second edition, 2023. ISBN 9789240067691. [Manual, corrigendum and worked example](https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240067691) · [2026 training package](https://www.who.int/publications/m/item/water-safety-plan--step-by-step-risk-management-for-drinking-water-suppliers--training-package).

Read the whole manual and the Aquatown example, then work the training activities against a documented supply. Connect hazards and control measures with operational observations, responsibilities, improvement and review. Compare the proposed response with the means and people actually available. Keep source-to-consumer risk management connected to design and routine operation.

The 144-page manual declares CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO with WHO's attribution, translation and third-party conditions. Its corrigendum belongs with the edition. The training package was published on 11 February 2026 and has its own component notices. A completed reading exercise is not evidence that a real supply has implemented its plan.

